In-game multiplayer (tools/web_wasm/net/sceneonline.cpp, netsync.cpp): the title's fourth entry (the LAN mode slot, which needs a broadband adapter the port does not have) is always offered and opens the MULTIPLAYER scene instead of SceneLanEntry. In a room the host's START takes everyone to the normal menus, which run in lockstep with one controller per player (port_netsync_scene at each menu scene's init; the player count is the room's; the menus' wall-clock random seeds use port_netsync_time). Course/map select hands the agreed race to netonline.cpp (port_net_race_begin before RaceApp::call) and the race returns to the multiplayer scene.

